WEBVTT

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:28.650
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:28.650
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:28.650
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:54.230 --> 00:02:02.650
The Mutineer
Chapter I

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:12.500
In August of Imperial Year 482...

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:16.050
...having achieved brilliant battlefield accomplishments in battle on Kapche-Lanka...

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:19.050
...and receiving a recommendation from the
base vice-commander, Commander Martel...

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:22.460
...Reinhard von Musel was promoted to Lieutenant Junior Grade(LTJG)...

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:25.460
...and transferred to an assignment in the Space Fleet, as he had wished.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:43.200
He was assigned to a
destroyer named Hameln II...

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:46.310
...and his duty was to be
chief navigator of that ship.

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:48.650
Kircheis was also
promoted to Ensign...

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:51.760
...and was assigned to be the
security chief of the same ship.

00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:54.420
There it is.

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:56.220
That's the Hameln II.

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:56.850
Right.

00:03:02.710 --> 00:03:08.220
LTJG Reinhard von Musel
and Ensign Siegfried Kircheis.

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:11.800
I see, LTJG Musel graduated from military preparatory school as valedictorian.

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:16.060
And did a superb
job on Kapche-Lanka.

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:17.000
That's quite impressive.

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:18.920
Thank you.

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:23.900
But needless to say, there's a difference
between ground warfare and fleet duties.

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:26.800
You're assigned as the
chief navigator to start with...

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:30.230
...but if you have any questions, be sure to ask for the guidance of Lt. Beltram here.

00:03:31.670 --> 00:03:32.420
Yes, sir.

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:33.420
I'm honored to meet you.

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:36.250
I'm the First Officer, Beltram.

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:37.010
Nice to meet you.

00:03:40.710 --> 00:03:44.260
The Lieutenant also graduated from the
military academy with impressive grades...

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:46.610
...and has since gained
much experience in the field.

00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:48.180
He's an excellent officer.

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:53.150
I leave all the actual duties to him, and I'm having an easy time.

00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:01.200
What is the Captain's personality like ?

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:02.500
Huh ?

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:04.100
He's a reasonable person.

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:08.750
Even though he's the successor of a Baronial family he's not arrogant and respects his subordinates.

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:10.870
As a superior, he's
easy to get along with.

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:15.650
Being the successor of a Baronial family and only a Lt. Commander at his age...

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:17.450
...he's certainly slow
getting promoted.

00:04:17.450 --> 00:04:19.700
I suppose that means
he's not very competent.

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:23.100
He didn't start
out in the military.

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:27.150
He used to captain a merchant
ship and joined the military later.

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:31.900
I suppose that because of it, he listens
well to born-and-bred servicemen like us.

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:35.530
I'll introduce you to everyone.

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:39.430
Everyone, remain at your
stations and pay attention.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:44.990
I'll introduce you to our new
chief navigator and security chief.

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:50.290
LTJG Reinhard von Musel
and Ensign Siegfried Kircheis.

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:53.250
They're young, but they're talented men with actual battlefield accomplishments.

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:55.100
Let's welcome them.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:59.580
LTJG, Ensign, this is our ship's
chief gunner, LTJG Shamissoe.

00:05:00.390 --> 00:05:03.780
That is our chief missileer, LTJG Dewling.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:06.540
Including the chief navigator, we call them the Three Field Chiefs.

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:11.080
Normally, the chief navigator is ranked above them, but on this ship, these two have been here longer.

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:13.210
Be mindful of that.

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:14.360
I understand.

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:18.420
Space Flight Operations, Ensign Emerich.

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:20.850
Communication Operations, Ensign Frebel.

00:05:20.850 --> 00:05:23.510
{Reconnoitering}Radar Operations, Ensign Gunaist.

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:25.750
That's all for the
officers on bridge duty.

00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:28.650
As for lower officers and other
crew members, I'll introduce you later.

00:05:28.650 --> 00:05:29.650
Let's go.

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:36.890
Oh well, how pathetic that the
chief navigator is a little kiddy like that.

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:40.290
He's the much-rumored little brother
of Countess Grünewald, isn't he ?

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:43.000
I wonder what the heck
the brass is thinking.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:46.500
I guess it's an extreme case of 
favoritism in personnel management.

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:51.960
Well, we've got a solid First Officer, 
so the chief navigator can just be a figurehead.

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:54.570
He's good for decoration,
with that handsome face and all.

00:05:57.540 --> 00:05:59.160
This is the ship's surgeon,
Doctor Yaunzon.

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:02.250
His rank is also
Lieutenant Junior Grade.

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:07.370
Oh, I'd heard you were young,
but you really are young.

00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:10.110
It's fairly close to
my area of expertise.

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:12.310
Expertise ?

00:06:12.310 --> 00:06:16.410
Before I was drafted by the military,
I was a pediatrician in town.

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:23.850
Next, we'll go see
our chief engineer.

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:28.550
I assume you know the structure of our ship, but the engine room is on the lower deck.

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:34.030
Basically, the upper deck is for officers,
and the lower deck is for the enlisted.

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:37.370
The chief engineer, too, usually operates from the upper deck.

00:06:44.930 --> 00:06:45.490
This way.

00:06:55.150 --> 00:06:56.990
Sir, how can I help you ?

00:06:57.920 --> 00:07:00.200
I'm guiding the new
chief navigator around.

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:02.000
Chief navigator ?

00:07:02.660 --> 00:07:07.540
They are Chief Navigator LTJG von Musel
and Security Chief Ensign Kircheis.

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:10.970
Why don't you salute them !

00:07:15.140 --> 00:07:16.100
Let's go.

00:07:24.030 --> 00:07:26.680
That was the chief navigator ?

00:07:26.680 --> 00:07:29.300
Hey, Rolf, he looks
younger than you.

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:33.050
Why are we still second class sailors, when such a kid already is a Lieutenant Junior Grade ?

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:35.510
You're still a kid, too.

00:07:36.130 --> 00:07:37.230
But, Brother...

00:07:37.820 --> 00:07:40.700
Of course it's because
he's an aristocrat.

00:07:40.700 --> 00:07:42.700
His name's got the "von"
in front of it, remember ?

00:07:42.700 --> 00:07:44.930
They get promoted
faster than us commoners.

00:07:45.970 --> 00:07:48.460
Even so, isn't his
promotion too fast ?

00:07:48.460 --> 00:07:51.870
That elite First Officer
is just a Lieutenant.

00:07:51.870 --> 00:07:57.210
Even if he's an elite from a military school,
he's from a commoner background after all.

00:07:57.210 --> 00:07:59.150
They may be about
ten years apart in age...

00:07:59.150 --> 00:08:03.600
...but by the time that kid becomes a First Officer he may already be like the Captain or something.

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:04.870
The Captain, huh ?

00:08:04.870 --> 00:08:07.100
It's like a story from
high above the clouds.

00:08:07.100 --> 00:08:10.170
Aristocrats can get promoted just with their family names.

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:11.540
Life's easy for them !

00:08:11.540 --> 00:08:13.550
Our Captain is the best example of it.

00:08:14.650 --> 00:08:17.050
He's so obviously reluctant
to be on the battlefield...

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:21.230
...that he leaves everything up to the
First Officer and lets him do all the work !

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:23.860
It's still not the worst - at least
he delegates to the First Officer.

00:08:23.860 --> 00:08:27.330
I've heard that in other ships, captains who rose solely because of their family names...

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:31.820
...actually meddle in matters despite their incompetence and get their ships destroyed.

00:08:32.680 --> 00:08:37.650
But of course, we've got the commoners' star
of hope, the First Officer, so we'll be all right...

00:08:37.650 --> 00:08:39.260
...no matter who becomes chief navigator.

00:08:49.570 --> 00:08:52.000
This is our chief engineer,
Engineer LTJG Inmarman.

00:08:55.490 --> 00:09:00.900
Sir, did you hear anything
about the spare parts I asked for ?

00:09:00.900 --> 00:09:02.020
No, not yet.

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:03.340
Are they that bad ?

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:08.410
Well, it'll probably last this time around, but I can't guarantee anything for our next launch.

00:09:08.410 --> 00:09:09.240
Come take a look at it.

00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:22.290
This ship is so worn-out.

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:23.210
Yes.

00:09:23.210 --> 00:09:25.850
But the maintenance
seems to be thorough.

00:09:25.850 --> 00:09:26.610
True.

00:09:26.610 --> 00:09:30.140
And that First Officer,
he seems to be trusted.

00:09:36.520 --> 00:09:37.660
Did you hear about it ?

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:42.850
That kiddy's the little brother
of Countess Grünewald.

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:45.150
Countess Grünewald ?

00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:47.860
The Emperor's favorite woman ?

00:09:47.860 --> 00:09:49.480
That's what I heard.

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:50.910
It makes sense now, doesn't it ?

00:09:50.910 --> 00:09:52.150
Even for an aristocrat...

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:57.200
...a 16 year old kid, who doesn't even have a titular rank, is already a chief navigator.

00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:59.200
I knew it was strange.

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:00.530
I see.

00:10:00.530 --> 00:10:04.000
Hey, Schmitt, since you're
a university graduate...

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:07.150
...you're probably more qualified to
be the chief navigator, aren't you ?

00:10:07.150 --> 00:10:09.250
Your major was astrophysics, right ?

00:10:10.350 --> 00:10:11.760
It can't be helped.

00:10:11.760 --> 00:10:14.200
After all, I was drafted
from a liberal arts university.

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:16.820
We get to be first class sailors
after one year of service.

00:10:16.820 --> 00:10:21.230
There'll never be an opportunity for us to put our expertise to use, I guess.

00:10:21.230 --> 00:10:26.000
Rolf, if you had a beautiful sister
instead of a brother like this...

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:28.410
...you could have been a Lieutenant Junior Grade by now, too.

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:31.290
Sorry to be a "brother like this."

00:10:32.380 --> 00:10:33.450
As far as I'm concerned...

00:10:33.450 --> 00:10:37.000
...I wouldn't mind being the Emperor's concubine, but he might not like it.

00:10:39.050 --> 00:10:41.730
It's really an unfair thing.

00:10:44.050 --> 00:10:46.170
How's the new chief navigator ?

00:10:47.070 --> 00:10:50.800
He's a pure bred elite who hasn't learned to deal with frustration.

00:10:50.800 --> 00:10:53.340
I sense that feeling
of pride from him.

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:56.900
I can't judge his actual capabilities until we get into the field, but...

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:02.130
I have high expectations
of you, First Officer.

00:11:09.230 --> 00:11:11.530
What do you think, Kircheis ?

00:11:11.530 --> 00:11:13.760
It's a superannuated ship.

00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:15.350
It's not just the ship.

00:11:15.350 --> 00:11:18.000
Including the Captain, the ship as a whole has no energy.

00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:19.200
Morale is also low.

00:11:20.490 --> 00:11:22.000
It might be different on the battlefield.

00:11:24.210 --> 00:11:26.160
It was the same at B-III Base.

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:28.970
The air of the whole
Imperial Force is stagnant.

00:11:28.970 --> 00:11:32.130
The reformation of their consciousness will entail an unimaginable degree of difficulty.

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:44.900
On August 27th, the Hameln II, with 
Reinhard was assigned as chief navigator...

00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:50.600
...received patrol orders for the Iserlohn
Corridor with the 237th Destroyer Squadron.

00:11:57.040 --> 00:11:58.820
Secure the position of our ship.

00:11:59.560 --> 00:12:01.200
Confirm the positions of our allies.

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:03.000
Secure the predetermined position.

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:05.050
Confirming the position
of our allied ships.

00:12:05.050 --> 00:12:06.350
Next please.

00:12:06.350 --> 00:12:07.400
Securing the predetermined position.

00:12:18.330 --> 00:12:21.420
Well, an aristocratic blond
kiddy with blue eyes...

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:23.700
...has always been a typical
antagonist since old times.

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:27.550
But, Brother, you always say...

00:12:27.550 --> 00:12:31.760
...whether you're an aristocrat or a
commoner, you're still a human being.

00:12:31.760 --> 00:12:33.250
Of course.

00:12:33.250 --> 00:12:34.900
When this ship sinks...

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:39.400
...you'll be a piece of space dust all the same, whether you're an aristocrat or a commoner.

00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:41.120
In that sense, we're equal.

00:12:41.120 --> 00:12:42.250
That's not what I mean...

00:12:42.250 --> 00:12:43.760
Sounds like you're having fun.

00:12:47.180 --> 00:12:50.820
It seems you two don't
like the new chief navigator.

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:53.000
Not really...

00:12:54.550 --> 00:12:55.970
You were listening to us.

00:12:55.970 --> 00:12:57.650
Sir, you're being mean.

00:12:58.550 --> 00:13:00.600
I understand your
concerns very well.

00:13:00.600 --> 00:13:03.180
In any case,
LTJG Musel is still young.

00:13:03.180 --> 00:13:05.250
Rolf, he's two years
younger than you are.

00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:10.080
To tell you the truth,
I'm concerned myself.

00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:15.150
I can't rest without worrying
when we change the watch...

00:13:15.150 --> 00:13:18.150
...thinking that he probably
got the job through favoritism.

00:13:19.600 --> 00:13:23.490
So he's only getting promoted because he's
the younger brother of the Emperor's favorite ?

00:13:24.520 --> 00:13:26.680
I don't know about "only because."

00:13:26.680 --> 00:13:29.350
After all, it seems he's achieved some battlefield accomplishments in ground warfare.

00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:35.200
But even though graduates from military
prep schools usually start as junior ensigns...

00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:37.380
...he started as an ensign.

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:40.600
That's the same treatment as for
graduates from military academies.

00:13:41.360 --> 00:13:45.870
You can say it's unfair
that he's getting a head start.

00:13:46.330 --> 00:13:47.910
That's foul.

00:13:49.150 --> 00:13:53.650
But I'm not assuming that
LTJG Musel is incompetent.

00:13:55.200 --> 00:13:59.350
If he has the ability appropriate to the position, there's no problem.

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:00.100
Don't you think ?

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:02.570
You're right, but...

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:08.810
Of course, his competence will be tested
on the battlefield, whether we like it or not.

00:14:08.810 --> 00:14:12.520
But it'll be too late if we
find out he's incompetent then.

00:14:12.520 --> 00:14:16.890
It won't be just him, all of us might get dragged down along with him.

00:14:17.230 --> 00:14:24.300
In other words, you want to test his competence before we get into a battle, right ?

00:14:24.900 --> 00:14:27.170
I'm not saying that.

00:14:27.170 --> 00:14:33.090
But if an opportunity presents itself,
it'd be a good for the whole crew.

00:14:33.790 --> 00:14:35.460
Then I'll do it.

00:14:35.460 --> 00:14:37.250
Do you have a plan ?

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:52.800
Until the next scheduled contact, we'll close communications with Kissingen III.

00:14:52.800 --> 00:14:54.100
Shutting down communications.

00:15:00.250 --> 00:15:01.640
First Officer on the bridge.

00:15:06.100 --> 00:15:07.100
I will assume command.

00:15:08.150 --> 00:15:09.900
The First Officer
will assume command.

00:15:16.070 --> 00:15:17.500
It's time for shift change.

00:15:17.500 --> 00:15:19.500
Except for those on duty,
leave your posts and rest.

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:44.880
Please don't put up
your guard like that.

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:47.370
I only have a little favor to
ask of you, Chief Navigator.

00:15:51.460 --> 00:15:52.780
What do you want ?

00:15:53.800 --> 00:16:00.800
Well, Chief Navigator, this is my brother Rolf, a new sailor in the engine room...

00:16:00.800 --> 00:16:05.700
...and he hasn't finished his maintenance before departure and has to do some outboard work now.

00:16:05.700 --> 00:16:08.550
But he doesn't have
experience, so he's worried.

00:16:09.610 --> 00:16:13.760
We'd like to help him, but
we're not that confident, either.

00:16:13.760 --> 00:16:18.920
From what I heard, you do things like zero
gravity training at military prep schools, right ?

00:16:19.630 --> 00:16:24.180
And I heard the Chief Navigator
was a valedictorian.

00:16:24.180 --> 00:16:26.620
So can you help him out some ?

00:16:27.600 --> 00:16:29.090
You're beating around the bush.

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:31.500
You mean you want to
test my competence, right ?

00:16:34.040 --> 00:16:36.700
Your perceptiveness
makes me feel great.

00:16:37.960 --> 00:16:38.900
Alright.

00:16:39.610 --> 00:16:41.590
That makes me feel even better.

00:16:41.590 --> 00:16:42.510
Doesn't it, everyone ?

00:16:44.150 --> 00:16:47.100
Lord Reinhard, I'll do it.

00:16:47.100 --> 00:16:50.450
No, they want to assess the 
competence of the Chief Navigator.

00:16:50.450 --> 00:16:51.590
I'll do it.

00:16:51.910 --> 00:16:53.190
Lord Reinhard...

00:16:53.190 --> 00:16:55.390
You keep saying, "Lord, Lord."

00:16:55.390 --> 00:16:59.800
Are you a servant of the
Musel family, Ensign Kircheis ?

00:16:59.800 --> 00:17:02.220
That disgusts me.

00:17:02.220 --> 00:17:06.700
Whether you're an aristocrat or a commoner, we're human beings, all the same.

00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:10.870
You might think it's your natural right to be above other people...

00:17:10.870 --> 00:17:14.000
...but in the field, you can't stand above others unless you're competent.

00:17:14.850 --> 00:17:20.000
If you want to act superior, I want to see you prove your competence.

00:17:20.440 --> 00:17:21.650
That's right.

00:17:21.650 --> 00:17:22.450
He's right.

00:17:23.810 --> 00:17:25.630
It's okay, Kircheis.

00:17:25.630 --> 00:17:27.900
He's got his reasons.

00:17:27.900 --> 00:17:30.300
I should let him acknowledge
my merit rather than my words.

00:17:44.990 --> 00:17:46.610
I hope not, but...

00:17:47.720 --> 00:17:49.800
If you check it, I'll be safe.

00:17:52.210 --> 00:17:54.810
Aren't the amounts of oxygen and propellants too low ?

00:17:56.090 --> 00:17:57.610
We can't waste them.

00:17:58.330 --> 00:17:59.560
We've got a time limit.

00:18:01.590 --> 00:18:04.020
Lord Reinhard, I think we should...

00:18:05.150 --> 00:18:07.700
In case of an emergency, back me up.

00:18:08.430 --> 00:18:12.050
Because you're here,
I can take the risk.

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:22.510
Are you ready ?

00:18:23.960 --> 00:18:24.810
I'm ready any time.

00:18:27.380 --> 00:18:28.690
Then let's get started.

00:18:35.990 --> 00:18:37.200
The objective is easy.

00:18:37.200 --> 00:18:42.020
Just exchange the 7th and 9th thruster units on the C-block on the port side.

00:18:42.020 --> 00:18:43.600
The one who does it faster wins.

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:05.930
Space is beautiful.

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:11.650
Hey, you'll run out
of propellants later.

00:19:18.560 --> 00:19:19.480
How reckless.

00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:27.940
Dammit, Rolf.

00:19:28.870 --> 00:19:30.150
Hey, give me a hand.

00:19:30.150 --> 00:19:30.980
I'll go out, too.

00:19:31.740 --> 00:19:32.620
What's happening ?

00:19:43.120 --> 00:19:43.870
This doesn't look good !

00:20:44.470 --> 00:20:45.400
Why ?

00:20:45.400 --> 00:20:46.240
Keep quiet.

00:20:46.240 --> 00:20:48.020
My thruster is low on propellant, too.

00:20:48.020 --> 00:20:52.300
To move the two of us in the direction of the ship I'm calculating the right angle to the thruster.

00:20:55.160 --> 00:20:55.770
All right.

00:20:55.770 --> 00:20:56.940
Don't move your body.

00:20:58.800 --> 00:20:59.580
Go !

00:21:04.870 --> 00:21:06.750
My thruster's done for, too.

00:21:06.750 --> 00:21:08.310
But we've got acceleration.

00:21:08.760 --> 00:21:09.510
All right...

00:21:11.280 --> 00:21:11.910
What ?

00:21:19.080 --> 00:21:20.150
It's going away !

00:21:21.230 --> 00:21:22.090
We're okay.

00:21:26.560 --> 00:21:27.370
Lord Reinhard !

00:21:28.480 --> 00:21:29.850
Rolf, you idiot !

00:21:35.020 --> 00:21:37.470
Kircheis, I knew you'd come for me.

00:21:49.290 --> 00:21:51.190
You saved my life.

00:21:52.380 --> 00:21:54.800
Not really.

00:21:54.800 --> 00:21:58.220
I was also saved by Ensign Kircheis and Petty Officer Zaidel.

00:22:03.650 --> 00:22:06.440
Why did you save a commoner's life ?

00:22:06.440 --> 00:22:10.800
Whether you're an aristocrat or a commoner, you're a human being, right ?

00:22:12.070 --> 00:22:12.990
Huh ?

00:22:21.580 --> 00:22:23.360
I'm getting to like you.

00:22:23.360 --> 00:22:25.000
You're too good to be an aristocrat.

00:22:37.760 --> 00:22:40.510
But...was that movement coincidental ?

00:22:43.300 --> 00:22:46.920
Reinhard had a vague suspicion.

00:22:46.920 --> 00:22:48.100
Ever since Kapche-Lanka...

00:22:48.100 --> 00:22:52.020
...he may have become over-watchful of things that happen around him.

00:22:52.020 --> 00:22:57.560
Either way, it was an incident that foreboded
the beginning of a rough journey ahead of him.

00:22:58.380 --> 00:23:02.770
It was an occurrence in
August of Imperial Year 482.

00:23:01.250 --> 00:23:04.700
To be continued

